{#-
  Completion scaffold for a BASE model (issue #88, Phase 6 / rung 4b).

  No special tokens and no chat framing at all: the render is a bare
  JSON array of records, the kind of scraped data file pretraining is
  full of. Exemplar records ride in as assistant turns; the model
  simply continues the series. Grammar supplies form, pretraining
  supplies voice. User turns render as ZERO bytes — they exist only to
  satisfy the prompt API's turn-order rule and carry no content.

  Byte layout (load-bearing for prefix-cache continuity):
    system    -> content + "\n"     (optional steering text above the array)
    open      -> "[\n  "            (once, after any system text)
    assistant -> content + ",\n  "  (one record, then the next slot's indent)
    user      -> ""                 (nothing)
  add_generation_prompt appends nothing: the render always ends at an
  open record slot, and the model's emission lands exactly where the
  next re-render will place the assistant content. The array never
  closes — generation is always mid-document.
-#}
{%- if messages and messages[0].role == 'system' -%}
{{- messages[0].content -}}{{- "\n" -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- "[\n  " -}}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message.role == 'assistant' -%}
{{- message.content -}}{{- ",\n  " -}}
{%- elif message.role == 'user' or message.role == 'system' -%}
{%- else -%}
{{- raise_exception("completion scaffold supports system/user/assistant roles only, got: " ~ message.role) -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
